{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "label": "Supply chain (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_npm_provenance_attestation", "label": "npm provenance attestation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proves which commit and which workflow run produced the published bytes; verify with npm audit signatures in a project that has actor-ts installed."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_cyclonedx_sbom", "label": "CycloneDX SBOM release asset", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generated from the installed tree so you can answer \"was release X affected by advisory Y\" without reconstructing the closure from a lockfile you would first have to check out. The jobs landed after v0.16.0, so the first release cut by the current pipeline is the first to carry it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_trusted_publishing_oidc", "label": "npm Trusted Publishing over OIDC", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The workflow exchanges a short-lived GitHub identity token for a one-shot publish token, so there is no long-lived npm token stored anywhere and none to leak."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_dependency_graph_is_not_the_sbom", "label": "The dependency graph is not the SBOM", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "GitHub dependency graph does not resolve the root Bun lockfile \u2014 it records unresolved ranges from package.json and misses transitives entirely \u2014 so Dependabot alerts and dependency-review-action describe something other than what shipped."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_codeql", "label": "CodeQL analysis", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs on pull requests, on pushes to main and develop, and weekly; the weekly run is not redundant, because CodeQL ships new queries continuously and a file clean when written can be flagged months later with nobody having touched it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_advisory_gate", "label": "bun audit advisory gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reads bun.lock, so it sees the versions that actually ship \u2014 the whole reason it is not dependency-review-action. It also runs weekly, because an advisory is published upstream against a lockfile that did not change and a push-triggered gate would not notice until the next unrelated commit."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_pinned_actions", "label": "SHA-pinned actions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A tag is a mutable pointer: whoever can move actions/checkout@v7 runs arbitrary code inside the job that publishes to npm. The trailing release-tag comment is what keeps Dependabot updating the pins, and a test asserts it on every run because workflow YAML is invisible to the type checker."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_frozen_installs_least_privilege", "label": "Frozen installs and least privilege", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every CI install is frozen-lockfile so a green check never means \"passed against a dependency set nobody can reproduce\"; job tokens are read-only by default and no job that can write to the repository also runs third-party install scripts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_security_policy", "label": "SECURITY.md scope boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plain-TCP cluster default ships on purpose and is documented alongside the mTLS recipe, so it is not a vulnerability \u2014 a documented mitigation that does not deliver what it promises is."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_npm_provenance_attestation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_cyclonedx_sbom", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_npm_provenance_attestation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_trusted_publishing_oidc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_dependency_graph_is_not_the_sbom", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_cyclonedx_sbom", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_codeql", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_advisory_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/security/supply-chain.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_supply_chain", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_security_supply_chain_pinned_actions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, 